      "text": [
        " اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ «۝ ثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ وَ لْيُوفُوا نُذُورَهُمْ ۝» قَالَ «اَلتَّفَثُ حُفُوفُ اَلرَّجُلِ مِنَ اَلطِّيبِ فَإِذَا قَضَى نُسُكَهُ حَلَّ لَهُ اَلطِّيبُ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2667 - Humran narrated from Abu Ja'far (as) regarding the verse of Allah (swt), the Exalted:\n\"Then let them complete their prescribed duties and fulfill their vows\" (Surah Al-Hajj 22:29).\nImam (as) said: \"Tafath refers to a person's grooming, including the use of perfume. Once he has completed his rituals, perfume becomes permissible for him.\""
        ]
      }
